{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>But man</b> — Some say: <b>in his wealth</b> — this is his wealth, which is money; it will not lodge with him in his death, rather he will leave it, and it is <b>like the beast that perishes</b>, that they too die in their death." "<b>They are likened</b> — cut off. And the Jerusalem Targum says: the one, which is the particular, is likened to the general."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:19.957599571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}